@mati-gp Please note that you can, if you want to, use "local" for embeddings, and openai for all regular calls. Opendevin will work.

In the future, doing that will affect performance, I mean the ability of the agent to do the tasks, but for now I'm not sure how much it affects it (maybe for long-running tasks... maybe not a lot, I'm really not sure). That said, afaik embeddings are much less expensive than the regular calls. I doubt they contribute to costs in significant measure, but as you reported, they contribute to rate limits.

The way opendevin works now, we rely on some default behavior with rate limits for embeddings which isn't working well. We're working on this, and should have a better experience soon.

